#
# oscap-run-sce-script: OpenSCAP runs a script check of the CIS content
# through this file when it cannot run the check itself. On the appliance
# that is every time: OpenSCAP writes the checks under /tmp, and /tmp is
# noexec (CIS 1.1.2.1). Without this file each script check ends in
# "error". Ubuntu ships it only in openscap-utils, which also pulls in rpm.
# Every script check of the content is a bash script. harden.sh installs it
# in /usr/local/bin, where OpenSCAP finds it on PATH. See
# docs/codebase/appliance-cis.md.
exec /bin/bash "$1"
